(1) THE RIEMANN-HURWITZ DESCENT X_0(2p) -> X_0(p) (degree 3 = the 2-adic peel):
      p  g(p)  g(2p)  chi(p)  chi(2p)  R=3chi(p)-chi(2p)  genus drop
      3     0      0       2        2                  4          +0  (deg=3)
      5     0      0       2        2                  4          +0  (deg=3)
      7     0      1       2        0                  6          +1  <== LRC-14: flat g=1 -> spherical g=0 (curvature removed)  (deg=3)
     11     1      2       0       -2                  2          +1  (deg=3)
     13     0      2       2       -2                  8          +2  (deg=3)

(2) INTERPRETATION: R = ramification = the curvature the level-2 CONCENTRATES = the residual.
    The 2-adic descent (THM-580) peels n=2p -> apex p; geometrically = X_0(2p)->X_0(p) degree-3
    branched cover; genus (curvature) DROPS; the removed curvature R is the iota-odd residual
    (n=14: g 1->0, the removed genus-1 = f_14 = curve 14a, S56/HYP-3768). The descent BOTTOMS at
    the genus-0 (spherical, no cusp obstruction) apex X_0(p): the base case of the LRC descent.

(3) the (2,3,p) apex geometry (mac-mini HYP-3771) vs X_0-genus:
    (2,3,3): 1/2+1/3+1/3-1 = 1/6 -> spherical;  X_0(6) genus 0
    (2,3,5): 1/2+1/3+1/5-1 = 1/30 -> spherical;  X_0(10) genus 0
    (2,3,7): 1/2+1/3+1/7-1 = -1/42 -> hyperbolic;  X_0(14) genus 1
    (2,3,11): 1/2+1/3+1/11-1 = -5/66 -> hyperbolic;  X_0(22) genus 2
    (2,3,13): 1/2+1/3+1/13-1 = -7/78 -> hyperbolic;  X_0(26) genus 2
